        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lands Knocknagin Road, Balbriggan, Co. Dublin \r\n\r\nc.1.53ha - c. 3.78 acres \r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 14th of October 2026 \r\n \r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Potential \r\n\r\nLocation Balbriggan 4km, Jcn 6 M1, 3km, Lusk 14km, Drogheda 26km, Dublin 33km. \r\n\r\nThe lands are located on Flemington Road, 3km north of Balbriggan town. Population (2022) 24,322. Balbriggan is a coastal town in Fingal, in the northern part of County Dublin. It is approximately 32 km north of the city of Dublin, for which it is a commuter town. The town has excellent transport links, to include the M1, commuter train (on the BelfastDublin main line) and bus services to Dublin. The town is coastal and has a sandy beach, along with an array of amenities and sporting clubs. The large port town of Drogheda is a short drive where further amenities are to be found. Dublin Airport 25km. Laytown beach 10km. \r\n\r\nDescription Folio DN152820F\r\n\r\nThe lands are contained within folio DN152820F and amount to c.1.53ha - c. 3.78 acres. The subject lands are in one irregular shaped block. They are laid out in large open plan manageable division, with mature boundaries of hedging and trees. The lands are currently in grass of good quality, however, are very overgrown at present. They could certainly be improved to suit all types of farming enterprises. There is good road frontage on two roads. \r\n\r\nIdeal location for a one-off house, subject to the necessary planning. \r\n\r\nThe lands are being sold as seen and not subject to planning. \r\n\r\nCoordinates 53.623973, -6.226719\r\n\r\nViewing By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nSolicitor Jack Byrne, MDM Solicitors, 16 Lavitt's Quay, Cork\r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
